  I've found that if I build up my pet to "large" size, and scrabble for
every extra AC point, things then just work out by themselves.  The
tougher pet means fewer kills for your character.  That provides a soft
"ceiling" on your XL.  You'll still get experience from wimpy monsters
it's safe to kill and finishing off monsters your pet couldn't handle.

  Extra levels for your pet(s) won't make monsters tougher, either.

  Just watch your hit points.  Don't run when your hit points get low.
You should have bravely run away long before that.  The first time a
monster takes away a significant fraction of your max (say 15%) run
immediately.  You'll need that reserve to get to safety while handling
unexpected problems along the way.

  If you get two strong pets, you can stay by one while the other clears
the level for you.  "You hear some noises in the distance" means Fluffy
is playing with her food.  Finding Fluffy busily cleaning herself next
to a stack of items containing a !oObjDet and a mirror gives a nice warm
glow to the cockles of my stony black heart.

  This is really nice in on dark levels in the Gnomish Mines.  You'll
survive assassination attempts you'll never even know about.  Your pets
will have eaten all the evidence, including the assassin's name.  Better
yet, Phydeaux and Fluffy will happily carry non-cursed items to you.

  If you ever have a sad feeling, it's only for a moment.  That's why
you tamed extra meatshields^W pets, right?  (An Evil Overlord cannot get
too attached to sacrificial minions.)




